    "final_cot": "Image description: In the figure, there is a large right triangle ACB, AC is the horizontal base, CB is the vertical side, and AB is the hypotenuse and is labeled with length 18. Point D is on AC, AD is labeled 9, DC is labeled 6, so AC = 9 + 6 = 15. From point D, draw upward a vertical line segment DF, intersecting the hypotenuse AB at F, and right angles are marked at both D and C. Reasoning: Because DF and CB are both perpendicular to AC, DF ∥ CB. Triangles ADF and ACB share angle A, and corresponding sides are parallel, forming similar triangles. Therefore AD/AC = AF/AB. Substituting AD = 9, AC = 15, AB = 18, gives AF = 18 × 9/15 = 10.8.",
